{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0035", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$a, b : A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$a, b$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-limits-products-equalizers}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b2d6c545405dda46e52d0dc4f376e232837e6123bfe6cff1d87eb2ed783e6203", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d346a6a8c3719930c81f298399eee8a3be8808dae6e6c5e876be3274abdb681a", "source_text": "Lemma <REF_0001> shows that (2) implies (1). Suppose (3) holds. The fibre product over the final object is the product. If <MATH_0001> are morphisms of <MATH_0002>, then the equalizer of <MATH_0003> is", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1ae68b223b5d6a4321abfc2fd3ec4b6c36af0e33490d327b1de66ce61c55e407", "unit_id": "tag:0035:proof-p001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "display_math", "parent_tag": "0035", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n(A \\times_{a, B, b} A)\\times_{(\\text{pr}_1, \\text{pr}_2), A \\times A, \\Delta} A.\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7dc1958c33312bf12b730c1530064d8d1d2682c75ee66e4f5d0577f40970129", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:69034f67370b7801db221f1512f0a1e20596ee3b8d1611e0cd65824cacba0b48", "source_text": "<MATH_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f624e62d0a08cb4d4f7609fd8d992c88c0c527d3d910b8338b5f898e6261de67", "unit_id": "tag:0035:proof-display001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof_paragraph", "parent_tag": "0035", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b0881b4250db5fa5d9405a31d5f0019ec7e67c90a67609125a304afb282dba00", "source_text": "Thus (3) implies (2). Finally (1) implies (3) because the empty limit is a final object, and fibre products are limits.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:557f856795be923824e8aedca831a920b51c69eb08cc22f0c17509fa61796233", "unit_id": "tag:0035:proof-p002"}
